It was only a tiny detail that led me to this.%K%P
契机，来自于一些琐碎的事情。%K%P
Michihama Trading hired me solely because my CV mentioned\nKamata Trading as my previous place of employment. I was,\nof course, instantly assigned to their accounting\ndepartment.%K%P
拜『原·镰田商事经理部』的头衔所赐，\n被这间『道浜商事』录用的我，理所当然地进了会计部。%K%P
They hired me out of season, so rather than trying to\nslowly bring me up so I could familiarize myself with the\ncompany, they just put me where I could start working\nright away. A reasonable decision, all things concerned.%K%P
毕竟是中途被录用的，不经过培训之类磨蹭的环节，\n充分发挥至今为止的实绩才是明智的判断。%K%P
Still, I thankfully got a bit of extra education on my\nfirst week with some on-the-job-training during lunch\nbreak, and permission to look up the old company records\nduring after-hours.%K%P
然而，在最开始的第一周，\n我幸运地被给予了实习时间，白天接受工作培训，\n而夜晚则是得到了接触公司内各种资料的机会。%K%P
The files in their storage were much more disorganized\nthan what I was used to at Kamata Trading, but at least\nthere weren't as many.%K%P
资料室中的文件库，\n比起镰田商事来说，虽然文件有点乱，\n但是数量绝对要少得多。%K%P
For the first three days, I just skimmed through\neverything I could find. The next two, I spent time\nreading the ones I marked as of interest.%K%P
用三天时间大致翻阅了一遍，\n接下来用两天时间认真阅读挑出来的资料。%K%P
And...%K%P
然后…%K%P
A particular suspicion started to weigh heavier and\nheavier on my heart with each record I investigated, like\na snowball rolling down a mountain.%K%P
一度产生的疑问，\n在我每次搜集新的，不，是旧的资料的时候，\n都像滚雪球一样不断在我的心中堆积膨胀。%K%P
%LCChief
%LC部长
\dAre you sure you didn't just miss something?\d%K%P
「大概是你看漏了吧？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI can't say it's completely out of the question, but I\nchecked everything at least ten times.\d%K%P
「应该不会这样…虽然不敢断言，\n不过，我已经检查１０遍了」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC部长
\dDid you have Chief Hiragi and the others cross check\nthese numbers?\d%K%P
「和平木科长还有其他的成员进行交叉检查了吗？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dNo... not yet.\d%K%P
「那个…倒还没有」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC部长
\dYou're just wasting my time. Don't come straight to me\nwith unverified reports.\d%K%P
「太不像话了。\n你这个报告真是自以为是」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...I'm sorry.\d%K%P
「…实在抱歉」%K%P
After everything I'd done, they wouldn't even glance at\nwhat I had prepared. There was nothing I could do about\nit.%K%P
再怎么说，谁也没有看过我整理的资料。\n所以，即使被这么批评，自己也没有办法反驳。%K%P
%LCChief
%LC部长
\dYou're too concerned with the details and minutiae. We\nare different from megacorporations like Kamata.\d%K%P
「你太拘泥于小事了。\n我们公司和镰田那种大企业可是不同的」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh, I didn't mean it that way. I simply grew curious\nabout what was happening. On a personal level.\d%K%P
「不，并不是这个问题吧…\n只是我个人有些在意这个而已」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC部长
\dThat's even worse. I have no time to waste on your little\npersonal investigations.\d%K%P
「那就更不用说了。\n我可没有时间陪你的这种个人兴趣」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC部长
\dTsk, I overestimated you.\d%K%P
「你真让我失望」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI... am sorry.\d%K%P
「实在是、非常抱歉…」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC部长
\dI hired you because I needed more people who are able to\nlook at the big picture and come up with original ideas to\nhelp us in these turbulant times.\d%K%P
「我之所以录用你，\n是因为我们想要能够更好地观察大局，\n而且可以为我们公司设计能够获取真正利益计划的人才」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dYes...\d%K%P
「是…」%K%P
%LCChief
%LC部长
\dBut all you're doing is digging through our old records.\nI didn't hire you to be our personal tax office.\d%K%P
「结果你来了之后，却只是在挑公司过去的问题…\n我们雇用你不是要你来模仿税务部门的」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI am sorry for letting you down.\d%K%P
「辜负了您的期待…」%K%P
You had to know what the tax office did to be able to fool\nit, though.%K%P
为了逃避税务部门的追究，\n模仿税务部门是非常必要的啊。%K%P
But I couldn't just tell him that.%K%P
这话我当然说不出来。%K%P
%LCChief
%LC部长
\dThat's the problem with people that come from the elite.\nYou cannot adjust yourself to smaller-scale projects, and\nthe only thing you have is your inflated pride.\d%K%P
「所以说来自大公司的人…\n明明干不了什么符合公司规模的工作，\n反倒是自尊高得要命，真是麻烦」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'm sorry...\d%K%P
「对不起…」%K%P
I was pretty sure I left any pride I might have had at my\nprevious workplace.%K%P
自尊什么的，一年半前就早已经被击得粉碎了。%K%P
%LCChief
%LC部长
\dAnyway, it's about time you gave me some space. And from\nnow on, you do not have permission to approach me\ndirectly. If you have something to say, pass it on through\nyour department's chief.\d%K%P
「这下你也该下去了吧。\n还有从下次开始不许直接来找我。\n必须通过平木科长」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...I understand.\d%K%P
「………是」%K%P
What he said wasn't mistaken in the slightest.%K%P
部长所说的，实在是过于理所当然了。%K%P
Under normal circumstances, a new employee who was\nrecruited out of season -- and not even through head\nhunting -- was acting completely out of line by bringing\nhis opinions directly to the head of the company.%K%P
虽说是被中途录用但还是新手的、\n就连猎头都没有经过的、还在试用期内的准社员，\n突然就直接找部长谈判本来就是不可能的。%K%P
But I had to take inconceivable measures precisely because\nmy findings were... just as inconceivable.%K%P
正因为发现了不可能的事，\n也就没有办法采取不可能的方法了。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dExcuse me.\d%K%P
「失礼了…」%K%P
I could feel a multitude of looks -- with badly faked\ndisinterest -- pierce my stooped back as I slowly returned\nto my seat.%K%P
我弯下了腰、有气无力地返回自己的座位，\n背上承受着仅仅是假装漠不关心的数条视线。%K%P
Well, you couldn't blame anyone for getting curious and\nindignant about the fact that a new guy just had a public\nfight with the boss.%K%P
入社未满两周的新职员，\n突然就咬住部长不放，而且立刻就被击得粉碎，\n被好奇和轻蔑的目光盯着也难怪。%K%P
Still, thanks to this inconceivable action of mine, I\nlearned something very important today.%K%P
但是，拜这作为公司职员的非常识行为所赐，\n也有一些东西浮出了水面。%K%P
That this business was known about as high up as the very\ntop of the company.%K%P
至少，这件事有可能是部长也认识到了的，\n虽然并不想承认，但多半是真相的事实。%K%P
A sense of deja vu rose to the surface of my mind like an\nunwanted shudder.%K%P
不断沿着背脊爬上来的，是恶寒一般的既视感。%K%P
\d...Michihama Trading?\d%K%P
『…道浜商事？』%K%P
\dIf you want my advice, give up on them.\d%K%P
『你最好还是别去哦』%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
Well, now... Was this what Ms. Sawashima meant when she\nsaid that to me?%K%P
当时…你说这句话，\n到底是要表达什么深层次的意思呢，泽嶋小姐？%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAh...\d%K%P
「啊…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh, h-hello.\d%K%P
「呀、呀啊…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...Are you coming back from work now?\d%K%P
「…刚回来吗？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dY-Yeah. I'm back.\d%K%P
「嗯、嗯，我回来了」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAh, welcome home. Um, Mr. Laid-off...\d%K%P
「欢、欢迎回来。\n…呐，失业先生」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWhat about you? Are you leaving to deliver newspapers?\d%K%P
「美都子，你现在要去送报纸吗？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dWell, yeah, but--\d%K%P
「是这样没错」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dYou're getting up at four in the morning on Sundays.\nThat's tough. Are you sure you can handle it?\d%K%P
「周日也要四点起床吗…真是够呛的。\n你真的不累吗？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dLook, that doesn't matter right now. Can you let me--\d%K%P
「不是那个问题啦」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI know you, so I'm not worried about you skipping out on\nhomework, but I believe the way you spend your holidays\nhas an effect on your overall schoolwork.\d%K%P
「毕竟是美都子，作业的问题我是不担心啦。\n不过，你这假期的度过方式，\n感觉还是非常奇怪啊」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dYou're trying to evade the subject, huh?\d%K%P
「你在逃避我的吐槽吗？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAnyway, see you. Do your best at work.\d%K%P
「那么就请慢走了。\n今天一天，也要精神地…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dStop right there.\d%K%P
「喂」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...You're choking me, Mitoko.\d%K%P
「…很难受啊美都子」%K%P
She caught my tie and pulled my head down to her eye\nlevel.%K%P
领带被狠狠拽住，\n还有被强迫着对上了她的视线。%K%P
I couldn't stoop that far, so I had no choice but to kneel\nbefore her.%K%P
…不欠身的话很难受啊。\n腰已经被压到这个地步了。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dLook, there's a limit to how hard one can work, okay? I\nmean, you're free to do whatever you want with your time,\nbut this is crazy!\d%K%P
「刚一就职就立刻开始勉强自己了。\n再怎么说今天也是休息日，你工作太多了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAhaha...\d%K%P
「啊哈哈…」%K%P
Would she end up locking me in the room if I told her I\nwas once again planning to leave for work around noon?%K%P
要是老实说出今天从下午开始也要上班的话，\n大概就要被这么关在屋子里了吧。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI mean, there's nothing wrong with putting effort into\nyour job, but I don't want to see you push yourself so\nhard that you end up collapsing in front of me.\d%K%P
「那个啊，虽然努力本身是件好事，\n但是我啊，也不希望看到失业先生努力过头、\n线啪地一声断掉了喔？」%K%P
I feel like someone had said something like this to me\njust the other day.%K%P
就在最近，好像有谁对我说了几乎一样的话呢。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dYou've been dozing off all the time as of late, even mid-\nconversation. Am I that boring to be around?\d%K%P
「最近，一回过神来你就睡着了。\n和我说话有这么无聊吗？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh, that's not it. I doze off after the first beer during\nMr. Retired's parties, too.\d%K%P
「啊啊，不是这样。\n和老爷子他们宴会的时候喝了罐啤酒才睡得那么快的」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dDon't lump me together with everyone else.\d%K%P
「不要把大家和我混为一谈」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dEh...?\d%K%P
「诶…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dTh-Then what about Ms. Kaya? Doesn't she get angry if you\nsleep in front of her?\d%K%P
「再、再说了，和夏夜小姐相处的时候是怎样的呢？\n不好好应对她的话不会生气吗？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh, I keep falling asleep in front of her too, but she\ndoesn't get too upset with me. She says she doesn't mind\nbeing boring.\d%K%P
「啊啊，虽然我最近经常在说话时睡着，但她也不会生气哟。\n无聊什么的，她并不太介意」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...Jesus Christ, just how far is she willing to go?\d%K%P
「…真是够了。\n甜得牙快掉了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'm all right. I'm gonna be right back on my feet if I\njust sleep a little. After all, I'm still in my twenties!\d%K%P
「所以说没关系。\n现在好好睡一觉的话就能恢复得很好。\n再怎么说我还只有二十多岁…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dJust don't grow any taller.\d%K%P
「不要再逞强了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...I'm sorry.\d%K%P
「…抱歉」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAre you really okay?\d%K%P
「真的没问题吗？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dYes, I am. Besides, finally being able to have a chat\nwith you filled me with newfound energy. ...Thanks.\d%K%P
「嗯，没问题的。\n因为久违地和你聊了天，我又一次恢复了精神。\n…谢谢」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...It's only natural to worry about your guardian!\d%K%P
「…担心监护人是被监护人的义务嘛」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\d\dI feel better after talking you for the first time in a\nwhile. Thanks.\d\d%K%P
「因为久违地和你聊了天，我又一次恢复了精神。\n…谢谢」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...You were listening?\d%K%P
「…听到了吗」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dMy, look at this! You're so nice! Only to her, though...\d%K%P
「真～好啊～，真～好啊～。\n只对房东小姐这么说～」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWhat kind of spoiled brat are you...?\d%K%P
「你是在耍小孩儿脾气吗」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dI can be whatever you want. A pure maiden, a ripe\nvixen... Just say the word and I'll do it.\d%K%P
「处女也好少女也好妓女也好淑女也好，都如你所盼」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'd rather not have either right now.\d%K%P
「哪个我都没在盼着就是了…」%K%P
Honestly... Ms. Kaya was such a...%K%P
唔～嗯，对夏夜小姐来说也真是…%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dHmph.\d%K%P
「切～」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAlso, I believe I've already told you, but this is my\nroom.\d%K%P
「而且，记得之前我也和你说过，\n这里是我的房间」%K%P
I was sure I counted the fourth door from the left, but\nfor some reason, I found the resident of Room #5 inside.%K%P
要是进入从左边开始数的第四个房间的话，\n就会看到本来应该在第五个房间里的人在那里。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dWell, y'know, we've been drinking at Mr. Retired's place,\nand I got lost on my way back.\d%K%P
「不是啊～，本来是在老爷子的房间里和大家喝酒的，\n结果忘记了回去的路啊～」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dBut all you have to do is go in a straight line to get\nback to your room from his.\d%K%P
「可是从老爷子的房间到这里的路并不难认，\n只有这一条单行线啊」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dAll these rooms look the same, that's the problem. I keep\nopening one after another, only to find out they're not\nmine.\d%K%P
「长得差不多的屋子并在一起，所以我犯糊涂啦。\n我从头一间一间地打开屋门，一边说着『也不是这里』呢」%K%P
I feel like we would lose her forever if she accidentally\nstumbled into Yasunaga's room like that.%K%P
不过感觉要是她这样进入八须永君的房间的话，\n她就没法再出来了。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAnyway, I would really appreciate it if you could let me\nsleep.\d%K%P
「总之，我现在是要睡觉了」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dAww, c'mon! Let's have some fun! It's your day off, isn't\nit?\d%K%P
「诶～再玩儿会儿吧玩儿会儿吧。\n难得的休假嘛」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThis is too much...\d%K%P
「还请您饶了我…」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dI'm bored!\d%K%P
「无聊～」%K%P
And to think I'd just praised her for not giving me a hard\ntime.%K%P
明明才刚刚夸过她『不会生气』的。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dUm, Ms. Kaya, seriously...\d%K%P
「我说啊，夏夜小姐」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dThen how's this for a compromise: share some of the\ngoodies with me.\d%K%P
「那，给我调停费。\n一点就好，请让我也湿润起来」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dGoodies? What do you mean?\d%K%P
「你说湿润…怎么湿润？」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\d1. A lap-pillow. 2. Sleeping together. 3. A certain kind\nof crazy and exhausting physical workout before bed.\d%K%P
「１．膝枕\n２．在旁边陪着睡\n３．睡前做一种激烈的，让人疲劳的运动」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI really hope those second and third options were just\njokes...\d%K%P
「再怎么说２号和３号也是开玩笑的吧…？」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dYou could call them dummy choices to lead you to pick\none.\d%K%P
「也就是，为了让你选择１的假选项？」%K%P
Her thought process remained a mystery, as always.%K%P
还是和往常一样，说的话让人莫名其妙。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dOh c'mon, don't be shy. Come over here. It's all soft and\ncomfy, y'know. I mean, you already had a taste earlier,\nright?\d%K%P
「好啦，躺下来躺下来。\n很柔软很舒服哦？\n之前你也体验过吧？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dYes, I did, including the blizzard that followed after.\d%K%P
「不光是体验过…\n那之后的雪夹冰也包含在内呢」%K%P
I didn't know the flame of a sparkler could turn ice cold\nwith just a glare.%K%P
没想到在烟花的火焰之下，一道视线会变得如此冷淡啊。%K%P
But back then she understood it wasn't something I did out\nof my own volition, and cheered back up after we played\nwith the sparklers for a while.%K%P
但是，在那个时候，\n“那并不是我的意志”这样的辩解还是有效的，\n那之后大家一起玩线香花火，她的心情随之好转起来。%K%P
In this case, however, I would be the one making the\ndecision.%K%P
而这一次的情况，不管怎样掩饰，\n我本人的判断都要介入已经是无可争辩的事实了。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dSo what now? You can pretend to have lost consciousness\nif you want. I'll handle the rest.\d%K%P
「怎么办？\n你先失去知觉也可以哦？\n接下来让我一个人享受就好了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dUm, I would love it if you could listen to me for\nonce...\d%K%P
「不，所以说…」%K%P
I had to take a firm stand instead of being all half-\nhearted with her.%K%P
向着仍然保持这样暧昧姿态的夏夜小姐继续撒娇——\n必须得适可而止了。%K%P
Regardless of my ultimate decision, it was about time I\ntook responsibility for my actions regarding her.%K
毕竟不管是进还是退，\n对我来说，已经差不多到了必须要对这个人负起责任的时候了。%K
Please let me sleep on your lap
请让我…躺在膝枕上
Please wake me up around noon
请在天亮的时候把我叫起来
